<title>CANADA: MDS to supply Columbia/HCA.</title>
<headline>MDS to supply Columbia/HCA.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian health firm MDS Inc will announce on Thursday a deal to supply Columbia/HCA Healthcare Corp, America's largest health care provider, with medical equipment, a Columbia spokesman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Columbia spokesman Jeff Prescott said the Nashville, Tennessee-based firm and Canada's largest health and life sciences firm had an arrangement. Toronto-based MDS declined to confirm the news.</p>
<p>No figures were given. However, one equity trader called the deal to provide automated sample handling machines &quot;huge.&quot;</p>
